@Tratcher Thanks a lot Chris. The date bit is helpful.

This cookie limit is great info, though it's a bit out of date on Safari versions. "Per domain" gives me what I need for searching. 

I was already starting to look at ITicketStore, but my hand may be forced. Do you have any recommendations for preferred storage for cookies? I've only seen an in-memory example. I am using Redis for Session, but unsure if there's a security or implication over using this vs SQL.

@Tratcher Hey Chris - I have everything all set up, but I'm struggling to handle the storage of the `AuthenticationTicket` into Redis. Do you have any proper guidance for this type? 

I'm trying to serialize the model but I'm unable.

> Type 'Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.AuthenticationTicket' in Assembly 'Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.Abstractions, Version=2.2.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=adb9793829ddae60' is not marked as serializable.

```
public static byte[] ToByteArray<T>(T obj)
{
    if (obj == null)
        return null;
    BinaryFormatter bf = new BinaryFormatter();
    using (MemoryStream ms = new MemoryStream())
    {
        bf.Serialize(ms, obj);
        return ms.ToArray();
    }
}
```

Just came across that after posting. Works just fine. Thanks!

```
public Task RenewAsync(string key, AuthenticationTicket ticket)
{
    TimeSpan? expiresTimespan = null;

    if (ticket.Properties.ExpiresUtc.HasValue)
        expiresTimespan = ticket.Properties.ExpiresUtc.Value.Subtract(DateTimeOffset.UtcNow);

    var ticketBytes = TicketSerializer.Default.Serialize(ticket);
    
    _cacheProvider.Set(key, ticketBytes, expiresTimespan);

    return Task.CompletedTask;
}
```

> > Yeah, ValidatePrincipal isn't great for that
> 
> Hm - I prototyped that as well and it seems to work fine (there is one little edge case that I need to fix)
> 
> https://github.com/leastprivilege/AspNetCoreSecuritySamples/blob/aspnetcore21/AutomaticTokenManagement/src/AspNetCoreSecurity/AutomaticTokenManagement/AutomaticTokenManagementCookieEvents.cs

I forked your sample & tried to make it match my solution, but I couldn't make it fail. 

I have a few extras at play:
- Redis backed ITicketStore
- Web & Api sharing cookies 

Api looks for the ASP.NET Core cookie on the request, and if found, it'll use the cookie policy. When it's not found, it'll use JWT. Defaulting to cookies gives me a big benefit due to the claims enrichment I'm doing for the user. When I use JWT (mobile app), that enrichment has to be done for each request.

If I only use JWT on the API, the `SignIn` within ValidatePrincipal works fine. When using cookies, I am finding the API cookie key seems to be out of sync with web. That's as specific as I can get right now as the semantics are over my head. That's when the the `ITicketStore.RetrieveAsync` call doesn't find the ticket given the key.

```
public Task<AuthenticationTicket> RetrieveAsync(string key)
{
    var ticketBytes = _cacheProvider.Get<byte[]>(key);
    if (ticketBytes == null)
        return Task.FromResult<AuthenticationTicket>(null);

    var ticket = TicketSerializer.Default.Deserialize(ticketBytes);
    return Task.FromResult(ticket);
}
```
